    Q1  Which parts of the complete session history should stay available across
        machines? Include the archived sessions, the tool_result records, and the
        full 日本語 transcript when deciding what needs to be kept. Assume one
        machine will often be offline.
    3 selected

  ❯ A ■ The complete transcript including all 日本語 tool records
        An offline copy keeps the full sequence of user and assistant messages,
        tool calls and their results. Copy it with the archive index, check that…
    B ■ Every exported summary and its original session index
        Read the session index first to find the full run. Retain the original
        summary with the exported version so edits can be compared offline.
    C □ 個別のツール結果と transcripts before each compaction
        Keep the tool_result records and intermediate summaries as they were
        written, including all of the Japanese test fixtures.
    D □ A backup manifest that names deleted or missing sessions
        Record which sessions were deliberately deleted, which moves are still
        pending, and whether the backup was verified on both machines.
